# Testing & Shipping Quality

Ship work as close to complete as practical: correct behavior, both locales, no secrets leaked, and tests covering the change.

## Required tests (default)

- Every meaningful change needs automated tests before considering it done.
- Prefer **PHPUnit** under `tests/Unit` and `tests/Feature` (already configured).
- Unit-test Services, Traits, pure logic; Feature-test HTTP / Livewire / auth flows.
- Keep tests focused and small — cover the change and critical edge cases, not the whole app.
- Run the relevant suite (`php artisan test --filter=...`) and fix failures before finishing.

## E2E (Playwright) — only when needed

- Browser E2E lives under `e2e/` with Playwright.
- Use E2E sparingly for critical happy paths (e.g. checkout, onboarding submit), not for every CRUD tweak.
- Prefer PHPUnit Feature tests when they can assert the same behavior cheaper.
- Do not dump full Playwright traces/logs into chat; report pass/fail + the failing assertion.

```bash
# Unit / Feature
php artisan test --filter=GuideStatus

# E2E smoke (when relevant)
npx playwright test
```

## Definition of done

- Behavior matches the request (happy path + obvious failures).
- New user-facing copy has `en` + `de` keys.
- No hardcoded secrets; billable APIs stay on-demand / bounded.
- Tests added or updated and passing for the touched behavior.
- No obvious pagespeed regressions (N+1, huge payloads, unused heavy assets).
